**CRITICAL**: Use Base UI components for consistent, accessible, and maintainable React interfaces.

## Base UI Library Integration - Core Principles

### Overview
Base UI (`@base-ui-components/react`) is a collection of high-quality, unstyled React components designed to be composable and styling agnostic. It provides accessible, customizable components that work with any styling engine.

**IMPORTANT**: The project includes custom form components in `@forms/` that leverage Base UI internally. These custom components should be used instead of the base Base UI components when available.

### Documentation Resources

#### Base UI Component Documentation
**ALWAYS** refer to the official Base UI documentation which is available in the shared/docs package:
  @shared/docs/base-ui/
**CRITICAL**: Always prefer custom form components from `@forms/` over base Base UI components for form controls. Use Base UI directly only for navigation, feedback, layout, and data display components.
**ALWAYS** consult the official Base UI documentation for proper component usage.
